; Bank $02 -- sound engine. Entry: the main loop pages in this bank and calls
; SoundRunFrame ($556A) once per frame. Backbone (verified by tracing):
;   SoundRunFrame  -- tempo gate ($cb6f frame-skip, $cb70 tick-repeat) -> run SoundTick N times
;   SoundTick      -- one tick: SoundStepAllChans then SoundUpdateAllChans
;   SoundStepAllChans  -- SoundProcessChan for each active channel (order WAV,PU1,PU2,NOI):
;                          advance phrase via channel cursors, read note/instrument/command,
;                          run the per-tick FX command (SoundDispatchFxCmd)
;   SoundUpdateAllChans -- SoundUpdateChan per channel: write GB sound regs / run tables
; Channels: hSoundChan ($FF8B) 0-3 = PU1/PU2/WAV/NOI -> rAUD1/2/3/4; KIT plays on WAV.
; Per-channel state is a struct-of-arrays at $C0xx-$C3xx (see constants/ram.inc wChan*);
; working read-cursors are 16-bit ptrs whose low bytes live at $C8xx (SoundInitStatePtrs
; sets them to channel 0, SoundAdvanceStatePtrs steps to the next channel).
494D SoundProcessChan     ; per-channel sound tick (channel = hSoundChan); called per active channel
49B7 SoundNoteToPeriod       ; wChanFreq[ch] = wNotePeriods[note+wNoteTranspose-1] (alt linear table at bank0 $09B9)
4C2D SoundAdvanceChanCursors ; advance the 3 phrase cursors (note/cmd, cmdval, instr) by c
4AA3 SoundWriteChanFreq   ; write the current channel's frequency to rAUDxLOW/HIGH each tick (no retrigger; P/L/V pitch)
; --- Note trigger: write the GB sound regs to start a note on the current channel
6007 SoundTriggerNote        ; dispatch by hSoundChan to the per-voice trigger below
604B SoundTriggerPu1         ; PU1 note-on: rAUD1 sweep/env/freq + trigger
6091 SoundTriggerPu2         ; PU2 note-on: rAUD2 env/freq + trigger
60D1 SoundTriggerWav        ; WAV note-on: rAUD3 level/freq + trigger
6014 SoundTriggerNoi       ; NOI note-on: rAUD4 len/env/poly + trigger
5151 SoundReadChanCursor     ; read byte via channel hSoundChan's 16-bit cursor (array base in hl); SRAM-guarded
485A SoundInitStatePtrs ; set $C8xx to the low-bytes of the engine's $C1xx state ptrs
; --- Note-on: load instrument from SRAM into wCurInstr, set up channel shadows -
5934 SoundSetupChan  ; dispatch by hSoundChan to the per-channel setup block below
5942 SoundSetupPu1      ; PU1: stage wCurInstr -> sweep/env/duty/freq shadows + trigger
5A27 SoundSetupPu2      ; PU2: stage wCurInstr -> env/duty/freq shadows + trigger
5B0C SoundSetupWav     ; WAV/KIT: stage wCurInstr -> wave level/freq shadows + trigger
5DB2 SoundSetupNoi    ; NOI: stage wCurInstr -> env/poly shadows + trigger
4F33 FillChan8         ; write a -> 8 consecutive bytes [hl] (clears a per-channel 16-bit array)
4F37 FillChan4         ; write a -> 4 consecutive bytes [hl] (clears a per-channel [4] array)
; --- Table macro playback (per-channel; runs the instrument's table) ----------
4668 SoundProcessChanTable ; advance/apply the channel's table (wChanTable/Played/Countdown); calls the column readers
574B SoundReadTableEnv  ; read table_envelopes[wChanTable][row] (song $1690 = SRAM bank0 $B690)
587D SoundReadTableTranspose ; read table_transposes[wChanTable][row] (song $3480 = SRAM bank1 $B480)
487E SoundReadGroove         ; read grooves[wChanGroove][wChanGrooveRow] (song $1090 = SRAM bank0 $B090) via wPtrGroove/wPtrGrooveRow
; --- Sequencer: song row -> chain -> phrase resolution ------------------------
48D2 SoundAdvanceSongRow     ; on wChanChain[ch]==$FF, walk chain_assignments (loop-back) -> next chain
5EAD SoundReadSongChain      ; e = chain_assignments[wChanSongRow[ch]][ch] ($B290 = song offset $1290)
5E7C SoundReadChainPhrase    ; e = CHAIN_PHRASES[wChanChain[ch]*16 + wChanChainRow] (SRAM bank1 $A080) -> wChanPhrase
; --- Per-tick FX command dispatch (command value in a -> FxCmdHandlers) -------
; Command values index the same table as the mnemonics at $0824 ("-ABCDEFGH...").
; B/D/G/H have null handlers here -- they act at note-trigger, not per tick.
4790 SoundDispatchFxCmd  ; a = command value (<19); jp FxCmdHandlers[a]
47A2 FxCmdHandlers              ; [19] dw: each command's per-tick handler (FxCmd_*; 0 = none)
4679 FxCmd_A            ; A: table start/stop
476C FxCmd_C            ; C: chord
46D8 FxCmd_E            ; E: amplitude envelope
46F7 FxCmd_F            ; F: wave frame / finetune
4812 FxCmd_S            ; S: sweep / shape
47C8 FxCmd_W            ; W: wave / duty cycle
4286 FxCmd_L            ; L: slide (legato)
69D7 EnvReleaseSpeeds   ; [8] envelope fade speed per release digit (SoundEnvReleaseSpeed)
6246 FxCmd_M            ; M: master volume
665F FxCmd_O            ; O: output (panning)
6646 FxCmd_P            ; P: pitch bend / shift
45D8 SoundApplyPitchBend     ; FxCmd_P tonal-channel impl: set up pitch bend from hFxVal (per-chan accum wChanPitchTarget)
43D8 PitchBendTable     ; [256] 16-bit exponential pitch curve; SoundApplyPitchBend reads [$43D8 + 2*hFxVal]
6669 FxCmd_T            ; T: tempo
649D FxCmd_R            ; R: retrig
65F3 FxCmd_K            ; K: kill note
7DD1 FxCmd_V            ; V: vibrato
7D81 VibDepthTable      ; [16] vibrato depth curve, FxCmd_V reads [VibDepthTable + (hFxVal & $0f)]
7D91 VibRateTableA      ; [16] 16-bit vibrato rate (type A); [$7D91 + 2*(hFxVal>>4)]
7DB1 VibRateTableB      ; [16] 16-bit vibrato rate (type B); selected by wChanVibType
7EAC KitPitchTable              ; per-pitch kit sample step deltas (SoundSetKitParams)

; --- context-based names (callee-derived role; Func/Proc = purpose TBD) ---
4000 SoundFxParsePitchVal         ; parse an FX value (mask $80/$0f) -> SoundInitEnv
4033 SoundKitStepLoopWin1         ; kit S cmd, voice 1: the high digit shifts the loop window (+/- digit*16, each edge clamped to the sample), the low digit moves its end (kept $10 past the start), then the read pointer is rewound into the window; FxCmd_S runs SoundKitStepLoopWin2 next
40E6 SoundClampKit1LoopEnd        ; clamp wKit1LoopEnd down to wKit1SampleEnd: a = 0 if it was past it, else 1
410C SoundClampKit1LoopStart      ; clamp wKit1LoopStart up to wKit1SampleStart: a = 0 if it was below it, else 1
4132 SoundKeepKit1LoopOpen        ; keep kit voice 1's loop window open: if wKit1LoopEnd is not past wKit1LoopStart, set it to wKit1LoopStart + $10
4154 SoundKitStepLoopWin2         ; kit S cmd, voice 2: SoundKitStepLoopWin1's twin over wKit2Loop*/wKit2ReadPtr (both call the other voice's start clamp: the ROM's cross-wiring)
4208 SoundClampKit2LoopEnd        ; clamp wKit2LoopEnd down to wKit2SampleEnd: a = 0 if it was past it, else 1
422E SoundClampKit2LoopStart      ; clamp wKit2LoopStart up to wKit2SampleStart: a = 0 if it was below it, else 1
4254 SoundKeepKit2LoopOpen        ; keep kit voice 2's loop window open: if wKit2LoopEnd is not past wKit2LoopStart, set it to wKit2LoopStart + $10
4276 SoundDivMod                  ; 16-bit hl / 8-bit c -> quotient in l, remainder in a (shift-subtract)
43CE SoundFxTableJump             ; FX dispatch via computed jump (jp hl region)
4637 SoundClampNoteRange          ; clamp a note value to playable range ($3c..$78) -> wChanDispNoteNoi
46C7 SoundClearChanFxSlots        ; clear this channel's 3 FX slots (wChanFxSlots/$c2f4/$c2f8 + ch)
472F SoundRunTableCol          ; dispatch one table column (-> SoundRunFxSlot / SoundRetrigNote)
4753 SoundRunChanFxSlots       ; iterate the 12-entry FX-slot table wChanFxSlots, run SoundRunTableCol per active
478D SoundDispatchStoredFx        ; load command from wFxCmd, fall into SoundDispatchFxCmd
483F SoundAdvanceTableCursor      ; advance this channel's table read cursor (wPtrPhraseRow ptr + wChanInstrPtr[ch])
48AB SoundAdvanceGroove           ; step the channel's groove row (wrap 15 / skip zero-tick), reload the note tick countdown
4B8A SoundReadChainTranspose      ; read chain_transposes[wChanChain[ch]] from SRAM bank1 ($A880, di/ei guarded) -> per-channel shadow wChanChainTranspose[ch]
4BC5 SoundTransposeNote           ; add chain transpose (wChanChainTranspose, song/chain mode) + global transpose to the note; skip if wChanTranspose set
4C26 AdvanceCurChanCursors      ; set de=hSoundChan*2, c=a (amount), then fall into SoundAdvanceChanCursors (advance current channel's cursors by a)
4C42 SoundAnyChanActive        ; scan the 8 wChanActive flags ($C0E0..7); return nz (flag in a) if any channel is active, z if none
4C4E SoundStartChan            ; handle wChanRestart (re)start request: read seq (SoundStartChanFromRow), set retrigger wPlayRestartPending, clear request
4C68 SoundLoadChanInstr        ; read the channel's instrument number from SRAM bank3 via its wChanInstrPtr[ch] cursor -> wChanInstr shadow (wChanActiveInstr/$c210[ch]); then SoundLoadInstr
4C9C SoundReadChainRow            ; read the current chain row (cp $ff = end-of-chain)
4CBF SoundAdvanceChainRow         ; advance the chain row, load that row's phrase; end-of-chain handling at row 16/$ff
4D71 SoundStepAllChans         ; run SoundProcessChan (sequencer step: advance phrase, read note/cmd) for each active channel, order WAV,PU1,PU2,NOI
4DA9 SoundEnterSongRow            ; commit wChanNextSongRow -> wChanSongRow, load its chain ($ff -> scan up)
4E17 SoundMaskLow5                ; return a & $1f
4E2A SoundDecodeNibbles           ; split a byte into hi/lo nibbles ($f0/$10/$0f)
4E69 SoundQueueSyncByte           ; store a byte to $cbdc / wSyncTxByte (sync transmit)
4E74 SoundDeactivateChan       ; clear wChanActive[ch] and wChanRestart[ch] (stop this channel)
4EA3 SoundResetFxState            ; clear retrigger wPlayRestartPending, wSoundTick, wSpeechWord, wPlayMinutes
4F2B FillChan16                 ; write a -> 16 consecutive bytes [hl] (staggered entry into the FillChan8/4 unrolled memset)
4F2F FillChan12                 ; write a -> 12 consecutive bytes [hl] (staggered entry into the FillChan8/4 unrolled memset)
4F3C SoundDecodeCmdNibbles        ; decode a command's nibbles ($01/$02 cases)
4FC0 SoundApplyTableCmd           ; (cp $02) SoundReadSramByteVia then jp SoundClampNoteRange
503C SoundReadSramByteVia         ; read [hl-pointer] from SRAM ($0a enable, di/reti) -> e
504A SoundRunTableStep            ; run a table step (SoundDecodeCmdNibbles, SoundNoiChordStep)
5074 SoundRandom15                ; randw() % 15: B (MayBe) in a phrase plays when this is below the probability digit
507F SoundAdvanceStatePtrs        ; advance the 7 working sound-state pointers (low bytes wPtrChainRow/e1/e3/e5/e7/eb/ed) to the next channel's slot in the $C1xx tables (counterpart of SoundInitStatePtrs)
509C SoundReadPhraseCmd           ; fetch phrase FX cmd+val for the current row (SRAM bank 2 phrase_fx); H/W special-cased
50E1 SoundReadTableCmd1           ; fetch table CMD1-column cmd+val via wTableCmd1Ptr/wTableCmd1ValPtr stream ptrs
5119 SoundReadTableCmd2           ; fetch table CMD2-column cmd+val via wTableCmd2Ptr/wTableCmd2ValPtr stream ptrs
5165 SoundReadCmdStream           ; read command-stream bytes (wSoundDataStride; cp $ff = end)
5345 SoundSetupWaveChan        ; ch2 (WAV/KIT): seed working ptrs (wPtrStepCountdown/e3/e5/e7/fc), SoundReadCmdStream
5459 SoundReadCursorByte          ; read a byte via wPhraseCmdPtr[ch] cursor + wPtrNoteSrc (SRAM-guarded)
5477 SoundTableHop                ; hop this channel's table to row a & $0F: the transpose and left command columns, or with bit 7 the right command column (its own row); e = 0 if already there
54D7 SoundUpdateAllChans       ; output phase of a tick: for each active channel (wChanActive $C0E0..7) set hSoundChan and call SoundUpdateChan (writes sound regs / runs tables)
556A SoundRunFrame                ; per-frame sound entry (called from main loop, bank00 $2317): tempo gate -- if wFrameSkip pending skip it; else run SoundTick 1+wTickRepeat times this frame
5583 SoundApplyTableTranspose     ; jp target from SoundStepTablePtrs: read table_transpose row, add to the channel note, apply (SoundTableHop)
55AE SoundCountdownStep           ; count down this channel's ticks left in the step: e = 0 if idle; at 0, flag the note trigger and advance the groove
55CB SoundReadChainEnd            ; chain end-marker check (cp $ff)
55EF SoundTableCmd1Hop            ; table command column 1's H: H0y hops to row y (SoundTableHop), Hxy counts x hops first (SoundDecodeNibbles)
5604 SoundTableCmd2Hop            ; table command column 2's H: as SoundTableCmd1Hop for the right column (bit 7 to SoundTableHop)
561B SoundReadGrooveOrSpeed       ; NB misnomer (no groove/speed access): if wChanTableFresh[ch], clear it (NOI: also wNoiTableNotePrev); else when wChanTableStep[ch]==0 step the 5 table read ptrs (wTableNotePtr, wTableCmd1Ptr, wTableCmd2Ptr, wTableCmd1ValPtr, wTableCmd2ValPtr) to the next row
5657 SoundStepTablePtrs           ; advance the channel's table step counter; on 16-step wrap rebuild SRAM read-pointers ($c1xx) for the table transpose ($B480) and command ($BA80) columns of wChanTable[ch]
56E1 SoundReadGrooveVal           ; table step 0 -> jp SoundAdvanceGroove unless the groove byte is $20; step 8 -> mark it $ff. (The trailing .initEnvPu1/.initEnvNoi stubs, zeroing wEnvStagePu1/Noi = ex-$cbbf, are separate entries.)
572B SoundInitEnv            ; init 3-node envelope for hSoundChan channel (WAV: none); stage=0, node1 -> vol+speed
5778 SoundSetKitParams            ; set kit state wWavSynthFrame/wWavRamDirty/wWavSynthEnd
583F SoundSplitPhraseNibbles      ; wChanPhrase[ch] -> hi/lo nibbles (compute phrase index)
58C7 SoundFillFF                  ; write $ff to a run of consecutive bytes [hl]
58EA SoundLoadInstr          ; copy the 16-byte instrument record instruments[a] (SRAM bank1 $B080+a*16) into wCurInstr ($C0D0)
5F5E SoundResetChanFx             ; reset this channel's (hSoundChan) retrigger rate, pitch slide and vibrato, and its LFO
5FA7 SoundResetWavFx              ; the WAV channel's part of SoundResetChanFx (retrigger, update flags, pitch rate, frame delta, vibrato)
5FBE SoundResetWavFlat            ; SoundResetWavFx, then a flat wave ($77 x 16) in hWavUploadBuf
5FDA SoundSetChanEnable        ; enable/disable this channel in rAUDENA (per hSoundChan; SoundWritePanning)
61A9 SoundWritePanning            ; set this channel's panning bits in rAUDTERM
61F7 SoundClearVoiceHram          ; clear $ffa0-$ffa3 (per-voice HRAM shadow regs)
6270 FxCmd_P_Step           ; P with PITCH on STEP: the pitch changes at once (a kit's rate by 3 a step, else wChanPitchCur by 8)
632B FxCmd_F_Wav                ; F on the wave channel: a synth's wave frame steps; a kit's two sample positions move (x16, doubled beyond +-16)
6479 SoundRandomUpTo              ; random 0..n (randw() % (n + 1); 0 for 0): the range Z adds to each digit
6577 SoundKillNote                ; kill this channel's note (K, now or when its slot's timer runs out): FX and FX slots, pitch slide, chord, vibrato off, table $FF
6685 SoundRunFxSlot               ; set hSoundChan = wFxChan & 3, run SoundKillNote
6694 SoundWavLevelStep            ; step the WAV output level (NR32 bits 5-6) by the signed high digit of the argument: negative towards off, positive towards 100%
66E7 SoundRetrigNote         ; R fires: play the slot's channel's latest note again (slide, envelope, table restarted), then reload or end the slot
68A0 SoundNoiPitchStep            ; the noise channel's pitch each tick: P's slide in quarter semitones, then V's offset, as note steps
6904 SoundNoiChordStep            ; step the noise channel's chord (C): the note, the first digit's offset, the second's (skipped when 0), the note again; SoundClampNoteRange gets the change
69C3 SoundEnvReleaseSpeed            ; E's release digit (hFxVal & 7) -> the envelope fade speed (EnvReleaseSpeeds)
69DF SoundEnvReleaseTarget           ; E's release direction (the second digit's bit 3, 9-F fade up): the volume the envelope fades toward, $0F or 0
69F2 FxCmd_E_Pu1                ; E on PU1 (from FxCmd_E): restart the envelope (retriggering when the length bit is set), then fade at SoundEnvReleaseSpeed toward SoundEnvReleaseTarget
6A28 FxCmd_E_Pu2                ; E on PU2, as FxCmd_E_Pu1
6A5E FxCmd_E_Noi                ; E on NOI, as FxCmd_E_Pu1
6A94 SoundLiveQueueStart          ; live mode: queue channel (arg) to start the song row's chain when its current one ends; again on the same row (chain/phrase screen) start at the edited chain row, sooner; with a sync restart pending, start now
6B59 SoundSetPlayRange            ; the channels to play (wPlayChanFirst..Last): the song cursor's column, or on the song screen in selection mode the selection's columns
6B9B SoundLiveQueueRange          ; live mode: queue a start for each channel in the play range (SoundLiveQueueStart)
6BBA SoundStartChanFromRow        ; start this channel playing from wChanNextSongRow ($ff -> stop path)
6D97 SoundStartChans           ; start channels [wPlayChanFirst..wPlayChanLast] from wSongRow (per-screen playback entry)
6E0F SoundStartRange              ; start the play range: queued behind what is playing if any channel is active (SoundLiveQueueRange), else at once (SoundStartChans)
6E24 SoundLiveStopRange           ; live mode, stop the play range's channels (SELECT+START): queued starts cancelled; an active channel stops at its chain's end, or its phrase's when pressed again (wChanLiveQueued)
6EA7 SoundLiveStartQueued         ; live mode: a channel queued to start (wChanLiveQueued) whose chain has ended starts now (wChanRestart)
6F65 SoundGetChainPhrase          ; bounds-checked chain_phrases[chain*16+row] lookup (chain=arg sp+6, row=arg sp+7 <$10; SRAM $A080); DebugTrap on out-of-range
6FB6 SoundStepWavFrames           ; step the synth's frames: on the timer, add the delta list's next step to wWavSynthFrame and reload the wave; at the list's end stop (play mode 1) or loop
7034 SoundSpeechStep              ; speech: when the frame's ticks run out, play the word's next allophone (SRAM bank 0 stream at wSpeechPtr; 0 ends the word) on kit voice 2, then read the next frame's length
70FB SoundEnableLcdInts           ; SetInterruptEnable
710E SoundInitPlayState           ; copy wCurScreen -> wPlayMode, clear wLiveMode, SoundTogglePlayback
711F SoundPhraseHop               ; H in a phrase: HFF stops the song; else, once a tick, go to the low digit's row of this phrase (after the high digit's count of hops) or, playing a chain or the song, of the chain's next phrase; e = 0 no hop, 2 stopped, 1 hopped
7362 SoundTableMaybeHop           ; B in a table (MayBe hop): with the high digit's probability (/16), hop to the low digit's row (arg: the right command column); e = 1 if it hopped
73B0 SoundZRepeat                 ; Z for a command slot (slot, last): repeat the last command that was not Z or H (wLastCmd[last]) with wLastCmdVal[last] + 0..each Z digit; e = the command
743E SoundZPhrase                 ; Z in a phrase (tail-jumped from SoundReadPhraseCmd): SoundZRepeat(hSoundChan, hSoundChan)
744D SoundZTableCmd1              ; Z in a table's CMD1 column: SoundZRepeat(4, 4 + the channel's table)
746F SoundZTableCmd2              ; Z in a table's CMD2 column: SoundZRepeat(5, $24 + the channel's table)
748E SoundReadChanStep            ; read the channel's next step: its note (or the PS/2 keyboard's), the groove's ticks less any D delay owed, its instrument (or the keyboard's), then the transpose (a kit note on WAV is masked instead)
75C6 SoundUpdateChan           ; per-channel processor (channel = hSoundChan): advance phrase cursor, resolve song/chain row, read note/cmd; called per active channel by SoundUpdateAllChans
77F0 SoundTick                    ; one engine tick: SoundStepAllChans (sequencer) then SoundUpdateAllChans (output); self-recurses on retrigger flag wPlayRestartPending / mode wSyncMode
786F SoundLiveChainEnd            ; live mode, at a chain's end: stop the channel if wChanStopQueued (the sound too once none plays), else start its queued song row (SoundEnterSongRow); e = 1 if neither
792B SoundStartSongPlayback          ; start the song, all four channels, at the song cursor's row: each channel's chain there, walking back past empty rows; from another screen's chain row (SELECT+START, sync OFF or KEYBD) each chain starts at that row, modulo its length
7B31 SoundStartScreenPlayback        ; start the current screen's playback: the song from the cursor row (SoundStartSongPlayback), or the edited channel's chain or phrase
7C4C SoundTogglePlayback             ; START: stop all playback, then start the current screen's unless it was the one playing (sync stop otherwise); live mode: SoundStartRange
7CFB FxCmd_E_NoteOn             ; E at a note-on (SoundNoteToPeriod): PU1/PU2/NOI stop the fade, the first digit sets wChanEnv (e = 5: the release runs); WAV sets wWavLevel (e = 0)
7F24 SoundSetupLfo                ; dispatch by hSoundChan -> SoundSetupLfoPu1/PU2/WavNoi (vibrato/LFO setup)
7F33 SoundSetupLfoWavNoi          ; LFO setup for ch2/3 (WAV/NOI): clear wEnvStageNoi, init from wChanEnvNoi
7F3E SoundSetupLfoPu2             ; LFO setup for ch1 (PU2): clear wEnvStagePu2, init from wChanEnvPu2
7F49 SoundSetupLfoPu1             ; LFO setup for ch0 (PU1): wEnvStagePu1, call bank0 SoundFadeEnvStepDown
78C4 SoundToggleSongPlayback         ; SELECT+START on any screen: SoundTogglePlayback as if on the song screen (all four channels); live mode: SoundLiveStopRange
5EDA NoiseFreqTable             ; [noise note] -> NR43 poly/divisor byte (120 entries)
5F52 SoundSetNoisePoly               ; a = NoiseFreqTable[a] -> rAUD4POLY (NR43); noise-channel pitch
7FF0 WavFreqTable               ; WAV channel sample-rate steps (FxCmd_P_Step)
7F51 SoundStepEnvToTarget            ; step channel volume [hl] toward e via zombie mode ($08 nudge up / SoundFadeEnvStepDown); c = rAUDxENV; shared tail of SoundSetupLfo*
7F5C .stepDown           ; target below current: fade one step down (SoundFadeEnvStepDown)

